 thing that they remember and they  all say that spider-man killed them with  the exception of sandman now here's  where we get the scene dr strange wants  to take them back to their original  dimensions but the villains feared that  returning would mean that they would  return to the exact same spot where they  came from meaning they would die and  here's the really important part norman  osborne manipulates peter into freeing  them making him feel guilty for their  deaths peter fights doctor strange and  breaks the key which is a cube which we  have seen in the trailer that held them  captive and the villains are now free so  what this tells us is that doctor  strange is holding them in some type of  prison he has some sort of cells prison  cells magical cells whatever you want to  call it holding them there and that is  the new leaked photo going around right  now and again it does include the leaked  pictures that we have seen in the past  so this new leaked photo is of this  scene the villains in their cells and  the interesting thing is that it does  look like they're in the sanctum in fact  it looks like they're in the exact same  spot where doctor strange performs the  spell in the trailer now in the trailer  around doctor strange and peter during  that moment we can see that everything  is kind of broken down and crumbles this  could be clever editing for the trailer  perhaps everything is fine but the  sinister six breaking out actually  caused some havoc and destruction and  that's what leads to some of this stuff  falling apart now of course it's always  hard to tell with marvel trailers  because they do things like this to  throw us off which is actually really  nice we don't find out everything from  the trailer because they're kind of  secretive with it but i'm gonna say this  is what's happening this leaked photo is  of the villains and their cells peter  and doctor strange fight and they  accidentally free them and the villains  cause a little bit o